       "elements": [
        {
         "id": "72aa7a6",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "heading",
         "settings": {
          "title": "Why the checks, and why they are printed",
          "header_size": "h2",
          "_css_classes": "gt-h2"
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "d0018f9",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "text-editor",
         "settings": {
          "editor": "<p>Looking for a therapist is hard enough without having to work out whether the person you are reading about is who they say they are. A counsellor is checked against a register that can strike them off. A coach, in the UK, has no register at all. A single “verified” badge across both would lend the credibility of the regulated professions to the unregulated ones, so Gototherapy does not use one. The badge says which checks were done for that role, and where there is no register, the profile says so.</p>",
          "_css_classes": ""
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "9ddceb1",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "text-editor",
         "settings": {
          "editor": "<p>We print the checks rather than asking you to trust us, because “trusted” is a claim and “checked on this date against this register” is a fact you can look at.</p>",
          "_css_classes": ""
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "be0273d",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "heading",
         "settings": {
          "title": "Why there are no reviews",
          "header_size": "h2",
          "_css_classes": "gt-h2"
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "bc46dfc",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "text-editor",
         "settings": {
          "editor": "<p>Reviews of therapy are not like reviews of a restaurant. They reward the therapist who was pleasant over the one who was useful, they cannot be verified without breaching confidentiality, and they push people to write about their own mental health in a public place. Gototherapy has no review or rating fields anywhere, by design.</p>",
          "_css_classes": ""
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "ea25bab",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "heading",
         "settings": {
          "title": "Why there is no enquiry form",
          "header_size": "h2",
          "_css_classes": "gt-h2"
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "29539ad",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "text-editor",
         "settings": {
          "editor": "<p>A message about somebody's mental health sitting in a directory's database is special category data that did not need to exist. You contact therapists directly, and what you say to them stays between you.</p>",
          "_css_classes": ""
         },
         "elements": []
        }
       ],
       "isInner": true
      },
